"business_notes": [
    "Revenue refers to the total billed amount generated from patient admissions.",
    "Insurance coverage represents the portion of the bill paid by the insurance provider.",
    "Patient payable amount represents the remaining amount to be paid by the patient.",
    "Department revenue is used to compare financial performance across hospital departments.",
    "Payment completion ratio indicates the percentage of successfully completed payments.",
    "Revenue band categorizes admissions based on billing amount.",
    "Financial risk is derived using billing behavior, insurance coverage and payment completion.",
    "Department revenue rank is recalculated whenever new billing records are processed.",
    "Average revenue represents the mean billing amount across admissions.",
    "High revenue admissions are identified using predefined business thresholds."
